The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (extended_tag_field_enable) {
    // Enable 8-bit Tags
}
```
```c
// Some devices do not handle 8-bit Tags as Completers
```
```c
// GPU lockup and unresponsive keyboards occur
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because certain Broadcom devices (HT1100, HT2000, HT2100) do not correctly handle 8-bit Tags when they are enabled, which violates PCIe specifications. This leads to improper processing of requests, resulting in system instability, GPU lockups, and unresponsive keyboards.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_SERVERWORKS, 0x0132, quirk_no_ext_tags);
```
```c
DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_SERVERWORKS, 0x0140, quirk_no_ext_tags);
```
Reason:
The fix involves adding quirks for the affected Broadcom devices to disable Extended Tags for the entire hierarchy. This prevents the devices from using 8-bit Tags, ensuring that they do not cause issues as Completers, thus stabilizing the system and preventing GPU lockups and keyboard unresponsiveness.

